.env.localWe already implemented the Appointments feature, but it was using in-memory seed data. Now backend is connected to PostgreSQL and returns persisted appointments. Update the mobile app to correctly fetch/persist appointments and update the Home dashboard to show recent appointments.

Scope (ONLY):
- Appointments feature (list + create + update + delete)
- HomeScreen appointments card content
Do NOT modify other features.

Backend expectation:
Appointments are account-level (not profile-level).
However, when listing appointments, we should still pass activeProfileId if API supports filtering later, but for now it should work even without profile filtering.

Tasks:

1) Update appointments API client (frontend)
- File: src/features/appointments/api/appointments.api.ts
- Ensure it calls the real endpoints and matches actual backend response fields.
- No mock/seed assumptions.
- Support:
  - list(params): GET /appointments?limit=&cursor=&from=&to=&status= (use params only if backend supports)
  - getById(id)
  - create(payload)
  - update(id, payload)
  - delete(id)
- Ensure date fields are handled consistently (ISO string).

2) Update React Query hooks (frontend)
- File: src/features/appointments/hooks/useAppointmentsList.ts
- Add support for optional params:
  - limit (default 20)
  - upcomingOnly boolean OR filter mode ("upcoming" | "past" | "all")
- Cache key must include params.
- On create/update/delete, invalidate list queries.

3) Fix AppointmentsScreen to show persisted data
- File: src/features/appointments/screens/AppointmentsScreen.tsx
- Remove any logic that assumes seed data.
- Show:
  - Tabs: Upcoming / Past / All
  - Upcoming sorted soonest first; Past sorted newest first.
- Use loading, empty, error states consistent with other screens.
- Ensure delete works and refreshes the list.

4) Fix AppointmentEditorScreen create/update to persist to API
- File: src/features/appointments/screens/AppointmentEditorScreen.tsx
- Ensure create uses useCreateAppointment mutation and returns saved record.
- Ensure edit mode loads detail via useAppointmentDetail then updates via mutation.
- After save:
  - navigate back to list
  - list should show updated data without manual refresh
- Use safe validation:
  - title/doctor required
  - startAt ISO required
  - location/notes optional
- Do NOT log PHI.

5) Update HomeScreen appointments section to show recent appointments
- File: src/features/home/screens/HomeScreen.tsx
- Replace the current "Manage Appointments" static row.
- Show the next 2 upcoming appointments (or latest 2 if none upcoming).
- Display:
  - Title or doctor
  - Date + time formatted
- Include "View all" which navigates to the Appointments stack route (same as current).
- Use existing design components (SectionCard/ListRow/etc.). No new UI libraries.

6) Backend check (minimal only if needed)
If backend routes still seed data or don’t query DB, update backend appointments module so:
- It reads/writes to PostgreSQL via existing ORM setup (TypeORM).
- Ensure endpoints return consistent shape:
  { id, title, doctorName, startAt, endAt?, location?, notes?, createdAt, updatedAt }
Keep backend changes minimal and limited to appointments module.

Constraints:
- Keep each edited/created file under 200 lines.
- Don’t touch navigation structure except if a route name mismatch breaks Home navigation.
- No unrelated refactors.
- Ensure Home and Appointments screens work after restarting backend and app.

After implementation:
- Create appointment on device -> it should persist -> relaunch app -> appointment still exists -> Home shows it.
